<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Fawn Lake from Crescent Lake Sno-Park</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:296-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="43.508945" lon="-121.969823"><ele>1459.9</ele><name>Crescent Lake Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin (OSM parking node 5136090498, just past the railroad on road 60); confidence: high; pdf_page: 298; quote: Crescent Lake Sno-Park is 2.2 miles from Highway 58. From the sno-park follow trail markers as the trail parallels the access road 0.3 mile</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.515410" lon="-121.983750"><ele>1505.7</ele><name>Junction with Fawn Lake Trail</name><desc>source: OSM node 5136109970, where unnamed path way 358442959 (from the Metolius-Windigo track north-west of the sno-park) meets Fawn Lake Trail #3844.1; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 298; quote: follow trail markers as the trail parallels the access road 0.3 mile, then turns uphill following an old roadbed for 0.7 mile. Turn right onto the forest trail for the final 2.4 miles</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.525120" lon="-122.006220"><ele>1720.5</ele><name>Fawn Lake, east shore</name><desc>source: west end of USFS trail 3844.1 FAWN LAKE at the lake; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 298; book_elev_ft: 5632; quote: winding about with ups and downs until you reach the lake. Ski to the east shore for a view of Lakeview Mountain to the west</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Fawn Lake from Crescent Lake Sno-Park</name><desc>1. Crescent Lake Sno-Park -&gt; Junction with Fawn Lake Trail: osm (medium), 1.01 mi | 2. Junction with Fawn Lake Trail -&gt; Fawn Lake, east shore: usfs-trail (high), 2.42 mi</desc>
